$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 1: Trifluoroborate
cross-couplings. To a microwave vial was added methyl
4-bromo-5-methyl-isoxazole-3-carboxylate 2 (1.0 eq.), the potassium
trifluoroborate salt 7 (1.0 eq.), Na2CO3 (2.0 eq.) and SPhos precatalyst
G2 (5 mol%). The vial was sealed, purged under vacuum and refilled with
N2 three times. EtOH (6 mL/mmol) was added to the reaction mixture and N2
was bubbled through the solution for 5 minutes. The reaction mixture was
stirred in an 85 °C heating block for 16 hours. The reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature, whereupon EtOAc (10 mL) was added and the
mixture was filtered through a short pad of silica gel, washing with 9:1
EtOAc/EtOH (100 mL). The filtrate was then concentrated. The crude
product, which was purified as specified. Ethyl
4-(4-fluorophenyl)-5-methyl-isoxazole-3-carboxylate 8a. According to
General Procedure 1, compound 8a was prepared from methyl
4-bromo-5-methyl-isoxazole-3-carboxylate 2 (480 mg, 2.18 mmol) and
purified by flash column chromatography (SiO2, eluting with 0-60 %
CH2Cl2/isohexane). Isoxazole 8a (378 mg, 1.34 mmol, 61 % corrected for
8:1 ratio of 8a:9) as a pale yellow oil, which was taken on into the next
step without any further purification. Ethyl
5-methyl-4-(6-quinolyl)isoxazole-3-carboxylate 8k. According to General
Procedure 1, compound 8k was prepared from methyl
4-bromo-5-methyl-isoxazole-3-carboxylate 2 (490 mg, 2.23 mmol) and
purified by flash column chromatography (SiO2, eluting with 0-50 %
EtOAc/isohexane). Isoxazole 8k (397 mg, 1.41 mmol, 63 %) as a pale yellow
solid, which was taken on into the next step without any further
purification. m.p. 56-58 °C; vmax (thin film)/cm-1 2983, 1735, 1612,
1592, 1570, 1500, 1454, 1378, 1352, 1328, 1295, 1226, 1199, 1177, 1121,
1025, 945, 930, 894, 859, 844, 800, 774; δH (400 MHz, CDCl3) 8.98 -8.95
(1 H, m), 8.18 (2 H, t, J 7.9), 7.77 (1 H, s), 7.66 (1 H, d, J 8.6), 7.46
(1 H, dd, J 8.2, 4.3), 4.35 (2 H, q, J 7.1), 2.50 (3 H, s), 1.29 (3 H, t,
J 7.1); δC (100 MHz, CDCl3) 168.6, 160.2, 154.0, 151.0, 147.7, 136.0,
131.3, 129.5, 128.8, 127.9, 127.2, 121.6, 117.0, 62.0, 13.9, 11.5; HRMS
(ESI+) C16H14N2O3 + ([M]+) requires 282.1004; found 282.1028 (-8.53 ppm).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
