$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Formyl-(3’’,4’’-ethylenedioxy)-5,2’:5’,2’’-terthiophene 7 (ETTCHO)
Firstly, boronic EDOT14 and 2-formyl-5’-iodo-5,2’-bithiophene3 9 were
synthesized according to the literature.
2-Formyl-5’-iodo-5,2’-bithiophene 9 (957 mg, 3 mmol) and boronic EDOT
(804 mg, 1 mmol) were dissolved in DMF (25 mL). Sodium carbonate (954 mg,
3 equiv.) and tetrakis (triphenylphosphine) palladium (0) (173 mg, 5%)
were added. The mixture was heated at 110 °C for 3 days. After return at
room temperature, the solvent was removed and the residue was dissolved
in dichloromethane. This suspension was filtered over celite. The
filtrate was washed twice with water and dried over magnesium sulfate.
The solvent was removed and the product purified by chromatography on
silica gel (eluent: dichloromethane).
2-Formyl-(3’’,4’’-ethylenedioxy)-5,2’:5’,2’’-terthiophene 7 (ETTCHO),
Yield: 63% (635 mg) - Orange powder 1H NMR (DMSO-d6): 9.87 (s, 1H, H1);
7.98 (d, 4.2 Hz, 1H, H3); 7.54 (d, 3.8 Hz, 1H, H4); 7.52 (d, 4.0 Hz, 1H,
H7); 7.22 (d, 4.0 Hz, 1H, H8); 6.68 (s, 1H, H15); 4.40−4.35 (m, 4H,
H12,13). 13C NMR (DMSO-d6): 183.6 (C1); 145.4 (C2); 141.8 (C10); 140.9
(C5); 139.3 (C3); 138.7 (C14); 136.0 (C6); 132.7 (C9); 127.3 (C4); 124.7
(C7 or 8); 123.5 (C8 or 7); 110.0 (C11); 98.9 (C15); 65.3; 64.2 (C12 and
C13). MS (M + H)+ calculated for C15H10O3S3: 334.9868 g.mol-1, found:
334.9870 g.mol-1.
