$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of
5-bromo-1-(phenylsulfonyl)-3-(pyridin-4-yl)-1H-pyrrolo-[2,3-b]pyridine
(1.0 g, 2.24 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (685 mg, 2.69 mmol), KOAc (660
mg, 6.72 mmol), and PdCl2(dppf)·CH2Cl2 (183 mg, 0.224 mmol) in anhydrous
1,4-dioxane was heated to 100 °C for 12 h under an atmosphere of N2. The
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was diluted with CH2Cl2 and MeOH and then filtered
through a short pad of silica (SiO2) and Celite, eluting with CH2Cl2 and
MeOH (30:1). The filtrate was concentrated in vacuo to give the crude
compound 4. The crude product was used for the next Suzuki coupling
without further purification. Brown solid, yield 590 mg, 57.1%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
