$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A N2-purged 10 mL two-necked flask was charged
with K2CO3 (276.4 mg, 2.0 mmol), triphenylphosphine (13.1 mg, 0.05 mmol),
palladium (II) chloride (4.4 mg, 0.025 mmol), iodobenzene (122.4 mg, 0.6
mmol) and a solution of 2-borylindole 7a obtained above in DME (3 mL).
The system was immersed in an oil bath at 80 °C. After 15 h, it was
removed from the oil bath and cooled to room temperature. The contents
were transferred to a round-bottom flask and volatiles were removed in
vacuo. The residue was subjected to column chromatography on silica-gel
(eluent; hexane/EtOAc = 5/1) (2-Furan-3-yl-1H-indol-3-yl)acetic acid
methyl ester, as white solid, yield 56%. Rf 0.43 (hexane/EtOAc = 2/1).
mp. = 107 °C 1H NMR (CDCl3, 270.05 MHz): δ 3.70 (s, 3H), 3.82 (s, 2H),
6.73 (s, 1H), 7.13-7.21 (m, 2H), 7.36 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.56 (s, 1H),
7.66 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 7.92 (s, 1H), 8.04 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
67.80 MHz): δ 31.0, 52.1, 105.5, 109.4, 110.7, 117.5, 118.9, 120.1,
122.4, 128.3, 128.8, 135.6, 140.3, 143.7, 172.4; IR (KBr): 3359 m, 2954
w, 1720 s, 1502 w, 1458 m, 1435 m, 1408 m, 1348 m, 1323 m, 1308 m, 1265
w, 1244 w, 1217 m, 1198 s, 1167 s, 1095 w, 1063 w, 1026 m, 1011 w, 991 m,
914 w, 872 m, 843 w, 771 m, 742 s, 721 m, 629 m, 590 m, 561 m, 445 w; MS
m/z (% relative intensity): 255 (M+, 52), 197 (15), 196 (100), 168 (21),
167 (28), 84 (14); HRMS Calcd for C15H13NO3 255.0895 Found 255.0896.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling
