$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.1. Synthesis of 1. To the solution of
4-iodophenol (1.1 g, 5 mmol) in toluene (25 mL), ethanol (25 mL),
5-formylthiophene-2-boronic acid (1.56 g, 10 mmol) and K3PO4·3H2O (2.67
g, 10 mmol) were added. Pd(OAc)2(58.4 mg, 0.6 mmol) was added under Ar.
The mixture was refluxed at 80°C for 8 h. After complete consumption of
the starting material, the solution was evaporated under reduced
pressure. The residual was purified by column chromatography (silica gel,
CH2Cl2 /CH3OH = 100:1, v/v). 3.14. Synthesis of BS-DS. The synthesis
procedure is similar to that of 1. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography (silica gel, n-hexane/CH2Cl2 = 1/1, v/v) to obtain
a red solid (45.1 mg), yield 54.4%. Mp:> 250°C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 7.51 (d, 3H, J= 6.6 Hz), 7.35-7.33 (m, 4H), 7.09 (t, 2H, J= 3.7 Hz),
6.86 (d, 2H, J= 3.5 Hz), 2.60 (s, 6H), 1.38 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 155.5, 141.0, 129.5, 128.2, 127.9, 127.4, 126.2, 29.9, 13.7,
13.1. TOF HRMS ES+ (C27H23BN2F2S2): calcd 488.1364, found 488.1385.
