$DATUM 1-(Cyclohexylamino)-8-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole-4-carboxamide
(39): Step 2: To
8-chloro-1-(cyclohexylamino)-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole-4-carboxamide (20 mg,
0.058 mmol),
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole (18
mg, 0.88 mmol), potassium phosphate tribasic (63 mg, 0.30 mmol),
Pd2(dba)3 (5 mg, 5.8 μmmol), and tricyclohexylphosphine (4 mg, 0.015
mmol) were added dioxane (3 mL) and water (0.16 mL). Argon was bubbled
through the solution for five minutes and then the reaction was heated to
100 °C until complete by LC/MS. Then, the mixture was cooled to room
temperature, diluted with ethyl acetate, washed with aqueous saturated
sodium bicarbonate, dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, and
concentrated. The residue was purified by HPLC to afford 39. Yield 12 mg,
0.031 mmol, 53%. LRMS (ESI) calc'd for (C22H25N4O) [M + H]+ 389.2, found
389.1. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CD3OD) δ 8.45 (s, 1H), 8.16 (s, 1H), 8.03 (s,
1H), 7.92 (s, 1H), 7.66-7.56 (m, 2H), 4.22 (s, 1H), 3.95 (s, 3H),
2.24-2.10 (m, 2H), 1.93-1.83 (m, 2H), 1.80-1.68 (m, 1H), 1.64-1.47 (m,
3H), 1.43-1.25 (m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
