$DATUM (6S)-6-[(6′-Fluoro[2,3′-bipyridin]-5-yl)methoxy]-2-nitro-6,7-dihydro-5H-imidazo[2,1-b][1,3]oxazine
(102). Reaction of bromide 160 and 6-fluoro-3-pyridinylboronic acid under
the Suzuki coupling conditions described in Procedure A, followed by
chromatography of the product on silica gel, eluting with 5% MeOH/EtOAc,
gave 102 (51%) as a yellow solid: mp 188-191 °C; 1H NMR [(CD3)2SO] δ 8.92
(d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1 H), 8.64 (dd, J = 2.3, 1.3 Hz, 1 H), 8.61 (dd, J = 8.2,
2.5 Hz, 1 H), 8.04 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1 H), 8.03 (s, 1 H), 7.86 (dd, J =
8.2, 2.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.31 (dd, J = 8.6, 2.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.77 (d, J = 12.3 Hz,
1 H), 4.75-4.67 (m, 2 H), 4.49 (br d, J = 11.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.33-4.22 (m, 3
H). Anal. (C17H14FN5O4) C, H, N.
