$DATUM Tetra(6-bromopyridyl)porphyrin 3: A toluene-DMF solution (6 mL/3 mL) of 2
(136 mg, 0.109 mmol), 2, 6-dibromopyridine (426 mg, 1.8 mmol), Pd2
(dba)3(3.0 mg, 0.0033 mmol), PPh3 (3.5 mg, 0.013 mmol), Cs2CO3 (126 mg,
0.39 mmol), and CsF (60 mg, 0.39 mmol) was degassed through three
freeze-pump-thaw cycles, and the reaction flask was purged with argon.
The resulting mixture was stirred at reflux for 22 h. The reaction
mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2, washed with water, and dried over
anhydrous sodium sulfate. After evaporation of the solvent followed by
GPC and silica-gel column chromatography (CHCl3 as an eluent) and
recrystallization with CH2Cl2 /MeOH, 3 obtained as a red solid (75 mg,
0.055 mmol, 50% yield). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 25°C): δ = 11.20 (s, 2H, meso-H),
9.19 (s, 4H, pyrrole-β), 8.22 (d, J= 7.8 Hz, 4H, pyridine-H), 7.90 (m,
8H, 4H for pyridine and 4H for di-tert-butylphenyl-ortho), 7.78 (m, 2H,
di-tert-butylphenyl-para), 7.60 (d, J= 7.8 Hz, 4H, pyridine-H), and 1.52
(s, 36H, tert-butyl-H) ppm; UV-vis (CH2Cl2): λ max (ε[M -1cm-1]) = 440
(190000), 547 (17000), and 581 (11000) nm; HR-MS: m/z = 1389.085[M+Na]+
(100%), calcd for C68H60Br4N8Ni1Na1 = 1389.088.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
